  "implemented": [
    "Public aliases, signatures, overloads, callbacks, arrays, member pointers, shared storage, fields and bases preserve unnamed template member nominal origins and native C++ values.",
    "Closed type, pack, template-template, enum integral, structural, declaration and null member-pointer arguments preserve ordered originating owners and exact converted values; template defaults and nested class/alias templates replay.",
    "Native anonymous member USRs use lexical ordinals under class-template owners, without source filenames or line/column dependence.",
    "Second providers project locked dependency types by reusing only previously admitted exact export identities and their template parameter owners.",
    "Capability admission rejects missing requirements and namespace-only projection owners; private originating owners remain rejected."
  ],
  "scope": [
    "The native backend is unchanged after the 237-unit/412-regression run. Final frontend and package reports bind the final facade and fixtures.",
    "Normal/eager/ASan+UBSan/TSan packages each cover C++20/C++23, ARC/MRC and O0/O2 after provider source deletion and package relocation. The full async fixture has one smoke configuration per normal/ASan/TSan mode.",
    "Runtime service and GNUstep binaries are reused unchanged from source 2.91. This batch changes public interface projection and native indexing identity, without modifying runtime or ownership/isolation lowering.",
    "The full five-family source/PCH runtime matrix remains recorded at source 2.91; it is not claimed to have rerun against this new native indexing build.",
    "Earlier failed reports remain distinct. A native-only witness reproduced the original counter failure: a by-value argument temporary lives through the whole conditional expression. The corrected witness checks cleanup in the following full expression. No compiler change was required for that failure; no SDK archive was rebuilt."
  ],
